```

This custom useToast composable relies on getCurrentInstance(), which only works during setup() and is considered an internal API. bootstrap-vue-next already exports a useToast() composable that provides toast.show() for exactly this purpose. Recommend using the library's composable directly rather than reaching through global properties.
```
import { useToast } from 'bootstrap-vue-next';
// ...
const toast = useToast();
```

`shouldRetry` is exported in useAllSubResources.ts (line 248). Import and reuse it:
```
import { shouldRetry } from '@/api/composables/useAllSubResources';
// ...
retry: shouldRetry,
```

The watcher fires on every change to any of the four reactive sources. If the query is already cached when the component mounts (e.g., navigating back to Overview after visiting Power), immediate: true will emit overview-power-complete instantly. Then any background refetch (if refetch options are enabled in the future) would cause isFetching to toggle false→true→false, emitting the event again.

The Overview page presumably uses this event to track loading. Emitting it multiple times may be harmless if the consumer is idempotent, but it's worth considering a once pattern:
```
const emitted = ref(false);
watch(..., () => {
  if (settled && !emitted.value) {
    emitted.value = true;
    eventBus.$emit('overview-power-complete');
  }
});
```

The "settled" formula on the overview card fires on the very first watcher invocation (with `immediate: true`), before any data is fetched.

Suggested fix — gate on the chassis collection actually being fetched and either the metrics being fetched or the URI being unavailable:
```
const { data: chassisMembers, isFetched: chassisFetched } = useRedfishCollection<Chassis>(...);
// ...
const settled = computed(() => {
  if (!chassisFetched.value) return false;
  if (!environmentMetricsUri.value) return true; // no chassis with EnvironmentMetrics
  return metricsQuery.isFetched.value && !metricsQuery.isFetching.value;
});
```
Then watch settled directly. (You'll need useRedfishCollection to expose isFetched, or expose it through usePowerControl.)

`metricsQuery.isLoading` is only true on the first ever fetch (pending + no data). On a navigation back to the page where data is cached, it's false from the start, so the loader never starts. That's probably desired (no flicker for cached data), but combined with refetchOnMount: true it means the user sees stale data and a silent background refresh.  
I think that approach is fine, but we should be explicit about it:

```
// Loader semantics:
// - First page load (cold cache): show loader until initial fetch resolves.
// - Subsequent visits: render cached data instantly; refetchOnMount runs in the
//   background without a loader. This avoids flicker on common navigation.
// - Mutations always show the loader, since the user is awaiting a save.
const isBusy = computed(
  () => metricsQuery.isLoading.value || mutation.isPending.value,
);
watch(isBusy, (busy) => (busy ? startLoader() : endLoader()), {
  immediate: true,
});
```

This is fine for production. The remaining cost is that a user who returns to the page after an external change won't realize they're looking at stale data for a second or two. For a power‑cap setting that changes rarely, that's almost always acceptable.

